questions.explanation:
Hint:\(I= I_z+I_{R_{L}}\)

Step: Find the maximum and minimum values of the current through the Zener
diode.
The current flowing through the circuit is shown in the figure below;

The total current in the circuit is given by;
\(I= I_z+I_{R_{L}}\)
where,\(I_z\)is the current through the Zener diode, and\(I_{R_{L}}\)is the
current through load resistance.
When the battery voltage\(V_B\)is\(8~\text{V}\), the total current through the
circuit is given by;
\(I= \frac{8-6}{1~\text{k}\Omega}= 2~\text{mA}\)
The current through the load resistance is given by;
\(I_{R_{L}}= \frac{6}{4~\text{k}\Omega}= 1.5~\text{mA}\)
The minimum current through the Zener diode is given by;
\(I_{z_\text{min}}= 2-1.5 = 0.5~\text{mA}\)
When the battery voltage\(V_B\)is\(16~\text{V}\), the total current through the
circuit is given by;
\(I= \frac{16-6}{1~\text{k}\Omega}=10~\text{mA}\)
The maximum current through the Zener diode is given by;
\(I_{z_\text{max}}= 10-1.5 = 8.5~\text{mA}\)
Therefore, the minimum and maximum currents through the Zener diode are
\(0.5~\text{mA}; ~8.5~\text{mA}\), respectively.
